-- title:
--   Level orbits and generators for a supersingular prolongation
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$ and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (this is `hA`, i.e. `A.LiesOverPrime q`); write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   **The level-$M'$ side.** `W` is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and its $M'$-substitution, over $\kappa$; here a place is a valuation subring containing the base field, different from the whole field, whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring. The hypothesis `hW` says that `W` consists exactly of the supersingular places, that is, of those places $w$ that are rational (the base field surjects onto the residue field of $w$), are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w(j)\in$ `ssJSet q κ` for the geometric $j$-generator `jGeomGen`. The hypothesis `hle` says that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, is contained in $F:=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H=$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   `R₀` is a constant reduction of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the latter whose kernel is the maximal ideal, lying over $A$ in the sense that a constant lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$ and reduces accordingly, with the scaling property, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with the divisors of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that `R₀` computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise residue of $y$. Finally `s` is a chosen element of `W`, and $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$.
--
--   **The prolongation and its chart data.** `FSS` is a field which is a $\kappa$-algebra, and `R` is a regular prolongation of $A$ from $F$ to `FSS`: a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `FSS` with kernel the maximal ideal, lying over $A$ on constants and compatible with the residue map of $A$, with the scaling property. `N` is a finite set of places of `FSS` over $\kappa$, and for every place $Q$ of `FSS` over $\kappa$ there are given a subring `Sx Q` of $F$, a ring homomorphism `φx Q : Polynomial ↥A →+* Sx Q`, a ring homomorphism `χ₀x Q : Sx Q →+* κ`, and a set `Dx Q` of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   **Hypotheses.** `h0`: some element of `FSS` is transcendental over $\kappa$. `h1` ($R$ lies over $s$): for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` is regular, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in `R.integers` and its `R`-residue equals the image in `FSS` of the value at $s$ of the `R₀`-residue of $f$. `h2`: for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, the pullback of `R.integers` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is `R.integers`. `hcard`: `N` has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   `hpkg` is the smooth-point package: for every place $Q\notin N$ the fourteen clauses, summarised here, require that the image of $A$ lie in `Sx Q`; that `φx Q` be formally smooth and formally unramified, send constants $C\,a$ to the images of $a$, and satisfy `χ₀x Q (φx Q (C a)) =` the residue of $a$ and `χ₀x Q (φx Q X) = 0`; that for each $c\in A$ with zero residue there be a unique character `Sx Q →+* ↥A` fixing constants, reducing to `χ₀x Q` and sending `φx Q X` to $c$; that every $f\in$ `Sx Q` lie in `R.integers` with `R`-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$ reducing there to the image of `χ₀x Q f`; that the `R`-residue of `φx Q X` have order $1$ at $Q$; that `Dx Q` consist exactly of the rational places $P$ of $F$ at which all of `Sx Q` is regular with values in $A$ and at which $A$-valuation strictly less than $1$ of the value of $f$ is equivalent to `χ₀x Q f = 0`; that each character `Sx Q →+* ↥A` fixing constants and reducing to `χ₀x Q` be the evaluation at a unique $P\in$ `Dx Q`; that for $P\in$ `Dx Q` regularity of $f\in F$ at $P$ be equivalent to $f$ being a quotient of elements of `Sx Q` with nonvanishing denominator at $P$; that a nonzero $f\in F$ of order $0$ at all $P\in$ `Dx Q` become a unit of `Sx Q` after multiplication by a nonzero constant of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and that an element of `R.integers` regular at all $P\in$ `Dx Q` lie in `Sx Q`.
--
--   `hdisj`: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, if some place lies in both `Dx Q` and `Dx Q'` then $Q=Q'$. `hcusp`: for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in$ `Dx Q`, the image in $F$ of the $q$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order at $P$. `heqv` (equivariance): for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of $F$ generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and given that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ` of `FSS` preserves $N$ (membership in $N$ is unchanged) and, for $Q\notin N$, carries `Dx Q` to `Dx` of the translated place, in the sense that $\{P:\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in \mathrm{Dx}\,Q\}=$ `Dx (R.resAut τ hτ • Q)`. `hUniq` (rigidity of the package): for every $Q\notin N$ and every quadruple $(S,\varphi,\chi_0,D)$ of the same shape satisfying the same fourteen clauses at $Q$, one has $D=$ `Dx Q` and $S=$ `Sx Q` as sets, and $\chi_0$ agrees with `χ₀x Q` on every element of both.
--
--   `hE1` (the Drinfeld identification with the level law) assumes `CoordRing q κ` — the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $\kappa$ by the Drinfeld relation — to be a domain for a given $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, and asserts that for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` there are a subgroup $C$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the Drinfeld actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta'\in C$) such that $\#C = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` and such that, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving `R.integers` through `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` and with $(\gamma \bmod q,1)$ in the kernel `hSubgroup q` of the character $(g,u)\mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$, the map $e$ intertwines the residual automorphism `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹)` with the Drinfeld action of $(\gamma\bmod q,1)$.
--
--   `hDLplus` is the corresponding statement with the inertia law adjoined and with the order of the quantifiers changed: for every ring homomorphism $\iota:\mathbb{F}_{q^2}\to\kappa$, used as the algebra structure, and assuming `CoordRing q κ` to be a domain, there is one subgroup $C$ with $\#C = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` there is a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) satisfying the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-intertwining, and in addition: for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the image of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup) and every $\alpha\in\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$ with $\iota(\alpha) =$ `A.tameCharacter π τ`, and for the semilinear automorphism $g$ of $F$ equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54), the automorphism $g$ preserves `R.integers`, and any ring automorphism $\varphi$ of `FSS` induced by $g$ on residues is intertwined by $e$ with the Drinfeld action of $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^{q})^{-1}),\alpha^{q})$ for every $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$ whose image in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ is $\alpha^{q+1}$, whenever that pair lies in `hSubgroup q`.
--
--   `haff` (affine chart off the ends): there is a subring $B$ of $F$ containing the image of $A$, contained in `R.integers`, contained in `Sx Q` for every $Q\notin N$, and such that every $z\in$ `FSS` lying in the valuation subring of every $Q\notin N$ is the `R`-residue of an element of $B$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The conjunction of the following five statements.
--
--   (1) The assertion `hE1`, repeated verbatim.
--
--   (2) The level group acts transitively on $N$: for all $x,x'\in N$ there are $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ such that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` preserves `R.integers` and the induced automorphism of `FSS` sends $x$ to $x'$.
--
--   (3) No place off $N$ is fixed by the whole level group: for every place $Q\notin N$ there are $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ such that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` preserves `R.integers` and the induced automorphism of `FSS` moves $Q$.
--
--   (4) Finitely many generators regular off the ends: there are $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and $g_0,\dots,g_{n-1}\in F$, all lying in `R.integers`, such that each $g_i$ is regular at every $P\in$ `Dx Q` for every $Q\notin N$ with value $P(g_i)\in A$, and such that every $f\in$ `FSS` lying in the valuation subring of every $Q\notin N$ belongs to the $\kappa$-subalgebra of `FSS` generated by the `R`-residues of the $g_i$.
--
--   (5) The assertion `hDLplus`, repeated verbatim.
--
--   This is a packaging step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ above a supersingular point of $X_0(M')$ in characteristic $q$: the component of the special fibre attached to the chosen supersingular place $s$ is identified, as a field with its level and inertia actions, with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$, and the statement records in addition that the $q+1$ ends form a single orbit under the level automorphisms, that every place off the ends is moved by some level automorphism, and that the affine ring of the component off the ends is generated by the residues of finitely many functions regular on the smooth-point discs. It feeds the constructor [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_igusaOverS_inertia_nodeCharts_hasseJ`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_igusaOverS_inertia_nodeCharts_hasseJ); the two middle conjuncts come from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_levelAut_transitive_ends_moves_smoothPlaces`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_levelAut_transitive_ends_moves_smoothPlaces) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart), while the Drinfeld identification laws pass through from the hypotheses.
